# vehje — Architecture Design

> General-purpose scripting language for game modding and embeddable
> runtimes. Game-agnostic core; game-specific surface ships as
> extension repos (`vehje-jomini` for Clausewitz, future `vehje-w3`,
> `vehje-ts4`, etc.).

## Status

**Initial seed.** This repo was extracted from the stellar-heritage
Python-implemented prototype on 2026-04-19. The Python implementation
(~15k lines, 1500+ tests) remains as a reference + parity oracle in
`stellar-heritage/tools/vehje/`.

The authoritative design spec is the seeded `mock/design_rounds/202604191300_topic.vehje-design-seed.md` (3095 lines). Grammar is in the grammar seed. See the changelist `mock/design_rounds/202604191301_changelist.initial-seed.md` for what's imported and what the first fresh session needs to consolidate.

## Two-language strategy

**Rust compiler + Zig runtime, joined by C ABI defined / validated in Rust.**

- **Compiler** (Rust): lex, parse, resolve, typecheck, transpile, codegen, scheduler. Runs at dev time. Distribution: single static binary. `#![no_std]` where practical, custom allocations.
- **Runtime** (Zig): executes macros, scratch variables, generative pipeline. Small, fast, embeddable. Talks to the compiler via C ABIs the Rust side defines + tests for soundness.
- **Build tooling / deploy / playset orchestration**: dogfood in Vehje itself (via the runtime), consuming the Rust compiler binary. rustc/cargo pattern — the compiler does one thing, the tooling runs on top of what we shipped.

## Substrate

- `arvo` (sibling repo) — numeric primitives + analysis (arvo-graph for pass DAG, arvo-bitmask for artifact read/write sets).
- `hilavitkutin` (sibling repo) — pipeline execution engine. Used by the Vehje *runtime* (morsel-driven execution of macros / scratch / generative), less so by the compiler itself (one-shot DAG walks don't need the frame runtime).

## Layers (finalised in first session)

The compiler crate split is TBD. Provisional:

```
vehje-lex        tokenisation
vehje-syntax     parser + AST
vehje-resolve    module resolution, use-tree, visibility
vehje-typecheck  coherence, bind targets, generics, validator framework
vehje-schedule   pass DAG (consumes arvo-graph)
vehje-codegen    target-agnostic codegen
vehje            top-level binary + orchestration
```

Runtime crate split (Zig side, TBD).

## Extension pattern

Game-specific targets land as separate repos that extend Vehje:

- `vehje-jomini` — Clausewitz (Stellaris / CK3 / HOI4 / Vic3 / EU4) grammar, bind targets (Country, Pop, Planet, …), codegen to Clausewitz script.
- `vehje-w3` (future) — Witcher 3 script target.
- `vehje-ts4` (future) — Sims 4 script target.
- `vehje-lua` (future) — generic Lua target.

The extension point contract is TBD (one of the first session's design rounds).

## Not in this repo

- Clausewitz-specific code, bind targets, content — stays in stellar-heritage until `vehje-jomini` repo exists.
- Python reference implementation — stays in stellar-heritage as parity oracle.
- Stellaris mod crates (std, stellaris, heritage, DLC-specific) — they're *programs written in Vehje*, not the language itself.
- Deploy / playset / artgen orchestration — belongs in stellar-heritage; eventually rewritten in Vehje as dogfood.

